# Decisions

**Status:** scaffolded

Why things are the way they are. One entry per decision, newest first, and an
entry is never edited once it has been made — a decision that no longer holds
is superseded by a later one that says so and links back.

This is the only document that answers "why this and not the obvious
alternative". Where the product is going is in the direction doc; what it does
today is in the product map; what shipped is in the changelog; what is proposed
is a PRD. None of those records a choice, and a project that never writes one
down relitigates the same argument every time somebody new reads the code.

Keep entries short. The alternative that was rejected and the cost that was
accepted are the parts worth having; the narrative is not.

